{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789250150,"nonce":"QSK8xlsmoqqV9Ufu3bCY1Rj/SxE=","title":"Async lowering ran liveness over every function of the module","message":"`apply_krio_async_lowering` and the resumable-effect lowering built an\n`AnalysisRunner` and called `run_all`, computing liveness and aliases\nfor every function, then read the result only for the async or\nresumable functions. A Python program with a large `__main__` (after\ninlining, thousands of values across a few hundred blocks) spent nine\nseconds in that analysis in a debug build, and under the parallel\nconformance suite that crossed the harness's 30-second limit, which is\nthe intermittent dict failure in 97592b3.\n\nFix: return early when there is nothing to transform, and analyse only\nthe functions that are (`AnalysisRunner::run_for`).","files":null}]}